🇺🇸 US Midterm Elections are Irrelevant 

▪️People banking on some sort of major shift in US foreign policy because of US midterm elections have failed to spot the obvious 21st century-spanning pattern of continuity of agenda and the absolute irrelevance of all US elections;

▪️The current US war of aggression under the Trump administration was prepared under the previous Biden administration, specifically with the collapse of Syria in 2024 without which the current war could not begin;

▪️The collapse of Syria was part of a proxy war started under Obama and continued under Trump's first term, and preparations for that proxy war began as early as the Bush administration;

▪️Foreign policy in the US is driven by unelected corporate interests, with politicians, Republican and Democratic candidates, the White House or Congress, simply performing theater to maintain false hope and distract away from continuity of agenda;

▪️If you plan on holding your breath for big change after midterms, you will turn blue first - if to want US foreign policy to actually change, start with the actual corporations driving it; 

▪️Expose the corporations - do not allow them to hide behind  political theater, direct your money, time, and attention away from them, and support instead businesses, organizations and institutions placing people and purpose above only profit.
